| A Forgejo epic's plan and features (#3835): an issue labelled `epic` has a Plan, its children the issues it depends on (Forgejo's issue dependencies, `/issues/:n/dependencies`), in steps by their own dependencies; **Add child** makes the epic depend on a new issue (level and feature labels) or one that is there, **Blocked by** makes a child depend on another; **Work ▸ Features** counts Forgejo epics by `feature:<name>` | Mac, web, Remote | built, tested on a scratch Forgejo | — | 2026-11-07, on a scratch Forgejo 11.0.16 in a container (the plan's reads and writes, and the Mac window and the web page), and against a stand-in Forgejo (`Go/internal/forgejomcp/forgeplan_test.go`, `Go/internal/agentsd/forgeforgejo_test.go`) | `Go/internal/forgejomcp/forgeplan.go`, `Go/internal/agentsd/forgeforgejo.go`, `Go/internal/agentsd/forgeplanwrite.go` | not yet on a real account (Codeberg: Alex's test, #3739); not on Gitea; no Board filter (no projects API in Forgejo 11) |
